# .trivyignore — the ONLY CVE escape hatch for the L4 security gate (Story 14.4 / ISI-2245, §6.2).
#
# This file is reviewed like code. Every suppression MUST carry, on the comment line directly
# above the CVE id:
#     <CVE-ID>   expires:YYYY-MM-DD   justification:<one line why this is accepted>
#
# The security.yml "trivyignore expiry lint" step FAILS the build when an entry is past its
# `expires:` date — a suppression is never a silent, perpetual mute. Remove or re-justify it
# before it expires. An unfixable finding still needs an entry (Trivy runs --ignore-unfixed, but
# a fix landing upstream turns a previously-unfixable HIGH into a gating one, so track it here).
#
# Format reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# --- active suppressions ---
# openssl CVE batch in the ksquad-console RUNTIME base (gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian12:nonroot,
# libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2, debian 12.13). Fixes exist upstream (libssl3 3.0.19/3.0.20-1~deb12u2 in
# bookworm security) and ride the next distroless tag rebuild; distroless has no package manager so
# the image cannot be patched in-repo. Remediation is external (upstream distroless base rebuild) —
# there is no open in-repo ticket: origin was ISI-2852 (done), renewal is ISI-4695. Durable action:
# remove these entries once the rebuilt base carries libssl3 >= 3.0.20 (check the runtime base pin in
# Dockerfile.console).
# Re-verified 2026-09-20 (ISI-4695): inspected the live nonroot manifest's dpkg status.d — the base
# STILL ships libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2, so the distroless rebuild has NOT landed and every CVE below
# is still present and unpatchable-in-repo. Renewed (not blind) to a fresh near-term expiry.
# Re-verified 2026-10-08 (ISI-4695 cadence): runtime base pin in Dockerfile.console is UNCHANGED
# (gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian12:nonroot) — no distroless rebuild adopted in-repo, so every
# openssl CVE below remains present and unpatchable-in-repo. Renewed to a fresh near-term expiry.
# CVE-2026-31789   expires:2026-10-28   justification:CRITICAL openssl heap overflow (32-bit X.509); runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-31789
# CVE-2026-28387   expires:2026-10-28   justification:HIGH openssl DANE TLSA use-after-free; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28387
# CVE-2026-28388   expires:2026-10-28   justification:HIGH openssl delta-CMS NULL deref DoS; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28388
# CVE-2026-28389   expires:2026-10-28   justification:HIGH openssl CMS processing DoS; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28389
# CVE-2026-28390   expires:2026-10-28   justification:HIGH openssl CMS NULL deref DoS; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-28390
# CVE-2026-45447   expires:2026-10-28   justification:HIGH openssl PKCS7_verify use-after-free; runtime-base-only, patch pending distroless rebuild of nodejs24-debian12
CVE-2026-45447

# --- ISI-3923: 2026-09 CVE batch surfaced by the Trivy DB across the toolchain images ---
# These are baked into UPSTREAM release binaries we download by pinned version (helm, kubectl,
# gh, dtctl, docker-cli) or bundled inside npm shipped in node:22-alpine — none are patchable in
# this repo, they clear only when the upstream tool ships a rebuild compiled with the fixed dep.
# All toolchain-image-only (no runtime/console exposure). Tracked by ISI-3923 (open remediation that
# bumps the pinned upstream versions / npm as patched releases land) — durable pointer for whoever
# hits the next red gate; the 2026-09-20 renewal itself is ISI-4695. Re-justify before expiry rather
# than blind-renew.
# Re-verified 2026-09-20 (ISI-4695): every pin below is UNCHANGED in-repo since these entries were
# written — helm v3.21.4, kubectl v1.36.4, gh v2.98.0, dtctl v0.38.0, docker:29-cli, npm 12.0.2
# (node:22-alpine), python:3.12-alpine. No upstream fix has been pulled in, so all remain valid and
# unpatchable-in-repo. Renewed (not blind) to a fresh near-term expiry.
# Re-verified 2026-10-08 (ISI-4695 cadence): re-grepped the Dockerfile.toolchain-* ARG pins — all
# STILL identical (helm v3.21.4, kubectl v1.36.4, gh v2.98.0, dtctl v0.38.0, docker:29-cli,
# npm 12.0.2 / node:22-alpine, python:3.12-alpine). No upstream fix adopted; all remain valid and
# unpatchable-in-repo. Renewed to a fresh near-term expiry.
#
